eck` already compiles the proof and prints errors.\n\n```\npython3 arena.py check --name \"{name}\"                # newest toolchain only (fast)\npython3 arena.py check --name \"{name}\" --all-versions # full robustness + score\n```\n\n`check` is the only scorer and the only compiler. Use `rg`/`sed` on the\ncorpus under `.lake/packages` to find lemmas. Do not use Lean MCP tools.\n\nLoop:\n\n1. At most **8** fast `check`s (no `--all-versions`) while you iterate.\n2. Then one `--all-versions`.\n3. **Stop** as soon as `--all-versions` shows every listed toolchain passing\n   **and** both `length_reduction_pct` and `heartbeat_reduction_pct` are\n   positive (below the references printed in the JSON). Leave that proof in\n   the work file. Do not keep golfing.\n\nIf `--all-versions` fails on one toolchain, rewrite for that failure and\nrepeat from step 2 (fast-check budget does not reset). Prefer a formulation\nthat works on all listed toolchains over a shorter one that does not.\n\n## When you are done\n\nLeave the final proof in the work file (last declaration in the file). Reply\nwith: what you changed, the final length and heartbeats versus the\nreference, which toolchains pass, and any rewrite that did not work.\n\nWRAPPER ID:\n36:WRAPPER_ID = \"v2-tight-loop\"\n197:    info: dict[str, Any] = {\"model\": model, \"effort\": effort, \"wrapper\": WRAPPER_ID}\n271:        \"wrapper\": WRAPPER_ID,\n305:    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)\n309:    p.add_argument(\"--name\", required=True)\n310:    p.add_argument(\"--version\")\n311:    p.add_argument(\"--force\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"reset to the reference proof\")\n314:    c.add_argument(\"--name\", required=True)\n315:    c.add_argument(\"--all-versions\", action=\"store_true\")\n316:    c.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=1800)\n319:    r.add_argument(\"--name\", required=True)\n320:    r.add_argument(\"--model\", default=DEFAULT_MODEL)\n321:    r.add_argument(\"--effort\", default=DEFAULT_EFFORT)\n322:    r.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=1800)\n323:    r.add_argument(\"--keep-work-file\", action=\"store_true\",\n329:    pr.add_argument(\"--name\", required=True)\n\nTrace files:\ntraces/distilled/20260817T224819Z-Cslib_CCS_bisimilarity_congr_choice.jsonl\ntraces/distilled/20260820T224127Z-Cslib_SKI_parallelReduction_diamond.jsonl\ntraces/distilled/20260820T224711Z-CallElimCorrect_extractedOldExprInVars.jsonl\ntraces/distilled/20260820T225546Z-Core_InitsUpdatesComm.jsonl\ntraces/distilled/20260820T230206Z-fundamental_theorem_of_variational_calculus'.jsonl\ntraces/distilled/20260820T231405Z-interleaved_affine_gaps_imply_tensor_gaps.jsonl\ntraces/distilled/20260821T201115Z-Cslib_SKI_parallelReduction_diamond.jsonl\ntraces/distilled/20260821T201800Z-CallElimCorrect_extractedOldExprInVars.jsonl\ntraces/distilled/20260821T202343Z-Core_InitsUpdatesComm.jsonl\ntraces/distilled/20260821T202628Z-fundamental_theorem_of_variational_calculus'.jsonl\ntraces/distilled/20260821T203211Z-interleaved_affine_gaps_imply_tensor_gaps.jsonl\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
